# ── Copyrighted source material — NEVER commit ─────────────────────────────
# The CBA PDFs and their full extracted text are © NBA / NBPA. They are large,
# re-downloadable (see tools/fetch_cba.py), and reproducing the full text is a
# copyright concern. Keep the raw corpus local; commit only DERIVED analysis.
#
# This rule is load-bearing here in a way it was not in the standalone nba-cba
# repo: data_explorer is PUBLIC. Same nested-.gitignore pattern as podcasts/.
corpus/
corpus/pdf/
corpus/text/

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# ── OS / editor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The Article I glossary is VERBATIM CBA text (88 terms, ~20 KB per agreement),
# not derived analysis -- so it falls under the same rule as the corpus above.
# It was committable in the private nba-cba repo; it is not here. Regenerate with
#   python cba/tools/fetch_cba.py && python cba/tools/build_index.py
# which writes it back into semantic/ (build_index.py:249).
semantic/*.definitions.json
